WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.527
Brody's eyes lit up. "There's a victory tour after the Games?" he said. "Cool!"

2
00:00:10.528 --> 00:00:18.142
But Julia was horrified by the news. "What do you mean?" she asked Artemis.

3
00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:26.709
The goddess shrugged. "Just what I said. The Olympic champion always travels with his sponsor afterward."

4
00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:32.000
"The tour gets mortals quite excited," Hermes added with a grin.

5
00:00:32.001 --> 00:00:37.292
He looked at Brody. "You'll enjoy seeing more of the world, won't you, boy?"

6
00:00:37.293 --> 00:00:42.826
"Sure!" Brody said. "It sounds like the parade after the Super Bowl!"

7
00:00:42.827 --> 00:00:45.640
Julia was staring at Hermes in alarm.

8
00:00:45.641 --> 00:00:50.057
"But you said we could go home right after the Games."

9
00:00:50.058 --> 00:00:56.681
"Of course you can," Hermes told Julia soothingly. "Don't worry so much, mortal girl."

10
00:00:56.682 --> 00:01:00.799
Julia glanced away, trying to calm down.

11
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:07.231
What if Hermes had been lying about letting them go home? What if they got stuck here forever?

12
00:01:07.232 --> 00:01:12.231
"This could be bad!" she whispered to Brody in a panic.

13
00:01:12.232 --> 00:01:16.180
"What are you talking about?" Brody asked.

14
00:01:16.181 --> 00:01:21.434
Julia kept her voice low. "What if Hermes is planning to keep us here?

15
00:01:21.435 --> 00:01:27.835
He and Caerus made it sound like the passage will eventually close. We could be stuck here forever!"

16
00:01:27.836 --> 00:01:30.845
"Whoa!" Brody said.

17
00:01:30.846 --> 00:01:36.970
For a second Julia thought she'd finally made him realize how serious this situation was.

18
00:01:36.971 --> 00:01:41.219
Then she saw that he was staring across the agora.

19
00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:47.087
"Who's that ?" he blurted out. Another goddess was approaching

20
00:01:47.088 --> 00:01:51.692
them. She was blond and gorgeous, with big blue

21
00:01:51.693 --> 00:01:56.442
eyes. "Greetings, Aphrodite," Hermes called. "Come and meet my

22
00:01:56.443 --> 00:02:04.597
champion!" Aphrodite held out one pale, slim hand. "Hello, champion. It's a pleasure."

23
00:02:04.598 --> 00:02:13.254
"Uh, guh . . . ," Brody said. "I mean, me too. I mean, hi! I'm Brody."

24
00:02:13.255 --> 00:02:19.446
"Brody," Aphrodite said with a musical laugh. "What a charming name."

25
00:02:19.447 --> 00:02:26.807
Julia moaned to herself. She could tell that Brody was already in love.

26
00:02:26.808 --> 00:02:31.097
Why were boys so easily distracted by a pretty face?

27
00:02:31.098 --> 00:02:36.284
"Have any of you seen Zeus' champion yet?" Aphrodite asked the other gods.

28
00:02:36.285 --> 00:02:40.537
"I hear he's very handsome. And strong."

29
00:02:40.538 --> 00:02:47.078
"Nobody has seen him," Artemis replied. "Zeus is hiding him in the hills."

30
00:02:47.079 --> 00:02:54.018
"That reminds me." Hermes grabbed Brody by the shoulder. "It's time for training. Let's go."

31
00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:59.587
"Are you sure we can't stay?" Brody was still staring at Aphrodite.

32
00:02:59.588 --> 00:03:06.922
Hermes pulled Brody away so fast that Julia and Markos had to run to keep up.

33
00:03:06.923 --> 00:03:14.527
Once again the gymnasium was filled with athletes. Hermes ordered Brody to start stretching.

34
00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:18.328
Brody dropped to the ground and touched his toes.

35
00:03:18.329 --> 00:03:22.128
"What are we working on today, Coach?" he asked.

36
00:03:22.129 --> 00:03:27.964
"We need to build your endurance for the dolichos and the hoplite ," Hermes

37
00:03:27.965 --> 00:03:34.878
replied. "They are the longer and more difficult races, and I wasn't impressed with how quickly you became tired

38
00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:41.057
yesterday." "Quickly?" Brody sounded wounded. "You made me run for two hours

39
00:03:41.058 --> 00:03:44.559
straight!" "We should get out of the way," Markos said to

40
00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.255
Julia. "It's strange enough to have a girl

41
00:03:47.256 --> 00:03:53.641
here. We don't want anyone to think you're trying to compete or

42
00:03:53.642 --> 00:03:58.188
something." He laughed as if that was the funniest thing he'd ever

43
00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:02.732
imagined. Julia was getting tired of all the comments about

44
00:04:02.733 --> 00:04:07.682
girls. "It's not as if I'm the only girl here," she said,

45
00:04:07.683 --> 00:04:18.595
pointing. Markos shook his head. "That's not a girl—it's a goddess," he said. "It's Demeter training her

46
00:04:18.596 --> 00:04:27.014
champion." "Whatever." Julia followed Markos to some benches. They sat and watched Brody's

47
00:04:27.015 --> 00:04:31.374
workout. After a while Caerus arrived and waved to

48
00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:36.012
Hermes. "Take a quick rest, boy," Hermes told Brody. "I'll be back

49
00:04:36.013 --> 00:04:43.814
soon." He hurried off to talk to Caerus. Brody collapsed on the bench beside Julia, huffing and

50
00:04:43.815 --> 00:04:49.783
puffing. As soon as Markos hurried off to get Brody some water, Julia turned to

51
00:04:49.784 --> 00:04:54.757
Brody. "Listen, we need to talk," she said

52
00:04:54.758 --> 00:04:59.734
quickly. "If Hermes isn't going to let us go after the Games, there's no reason to stick

53
00:04:59.735 --> 00:05:03.935
around. We should try to escape as soon as

54
00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:09.545
possible." Brody didn't respond. He was peering toward the

55
00:05:09.546 --> 00:05:13.234
entrance. "Do you think Aphrodite has a champion?" he

56
00:05:13.235 --> 00:05:16.730
asked. "Maybe she'll bring him here to train. Do you think she

57
00:05:16.731 --> 00:05:23.317
will?" Just then Markos returned with the water. He saw Brody staring at

58
00:05:23.318 --> 00:05:29.847
Aphrodite. "Forget her," he warned Brody. "She's beautiful. But she's a

59
00:05:29.848 --> 00:05:36.256
goddess." Brody looked disappointed. "So I guess goddesses never, like, date mortals,

60
00:05:36.257 --> 00:05:41.829
huh?" Markos blinked. "Of course they do. But it never turns out very well for the

61
00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:45.125
mortal." He glanced around and lowered his

62
00:05:45.126 --> 00:05:51.960
voice. "According to the latest local gossip, Hera is very eager to see Zeus' new hero humiliated at the Games.

63
00:05:51.961 --> 00:05:56.259
Alcides is rumored to be Zeus' child born of a mortal woman.

64
00:05:56.260 --> 00:06:00.110
And we all know how jealous and vengeful Hera can be."

65
00:06:00.111 --> 00:06:06.397
"We do?" Brody looked confused. "Okay, whatever. Back to Aphrodite, I—"

66
00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:10.734
At that moment Hermes rushed over, looking excited.

67
00:06:10.735 --> 00:06:13.783
"Apollo just arrived with his champion," he said.

68
00:06:13.784 --> 00:06:18.829
"He's challenged us to a javelin contest. Come—it'll be good training."

69
00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:23.158
"Javelin? I've never done that before." Brody shrugged.

70
00:06:23.159 --> 00:06:26.807
"But it's just throwing a stick, right? How hard can it be?"

71
00:06:26.808 --> 00:06:29.337
He followed Hermes.

72
00:06:29.338 --> 00:06:38.061
Julia watched them go. "I can't believe Brody's being so stupid about all this!" she complained to Markos.

73
00:06:38.062 --> 00:06:44.500
Markos gave her an uneasy glance. "Perhaps we should watch the contest in silence."

74
00:06:44.501 --> 00:06:52.829
Halfway across the gymnasium, Brody and Hermes met up with Apollo and a tall teenager with broad shoulders and dark hair.

75
00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:59.113
The two boys picked up javelins. Apollo's champion handled his confidently.

76
00:06:59.114 --> 00:07:06.385
Brody fumbled with his javelin at first, but within moments he looked almost as comfortable as the other boy.

77
00:07:06.386 --> 00:07:12.093
Julia couldn't help being impressed. Brody really was a good athlete.

78
00:07:12.094 --> 00:07:18.103
"Too bad he doesn't have much brainpower to go with his athletic abilities," she thought.

79
00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:20.837
"Go!" Hermes called.

80
00:07:20.838 --> 00:07:30.649
Both athletes tossed their javelins. Julia blinked as the javelins flew through the air. Something about them looked strange…

81
00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:36.980
She gasped as both javelins transformed into enormous hissing snakes.

82
00:07:36.981 --> 00:07:47.241
They spun around in midair and flew straight back toward the boys!

